{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-68352-r4520355","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Pepes Ikan (Indonesian Steamed Fish)","sourcePageId":68352,"sourceRevision":"4520355","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-29T18:20:55Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Pepes%20Ikan%20(Indonesian%20Steamed%20Fish)&oldid=4520355","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:20:18.668Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Indonesian recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using candlenut","Category:Recipes using carp","Category:Recipes using chile","Category:Recipes using fresh ginger","Category:Recipes using green onion","Category:Recipes using lemongrass","Category:Recipes using salt","Category:Recipes using sugar","Category:Recipes with images"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"8bdd2f1b10b1c9704aa10a77b3efabba9bad0c2d2ce273c38094e7947d43b0c9","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__{{Recipesummary\n| Category = Fish recipes\n| Servings = 4–6\n| Time = 60 minutes\n| Rating = 3\n| Energy = \n| Image = [[Image:IkanPepes.JPG|300px]]\n}}{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Indonesia|Cuisine of Indonesia]]\n\n''Pepes'' is cooking method of steaming the ingredients (fish, chicken, tofu, or mushroom) wrapped in banana leaves until it becomes tender, then grilling the packets. In this recipe any fresh water fish or salt water fish can be used as substitute. In restaurants serving West Java cuisine, where ''Ikan Pepes'' is always on the menu, the use of carp fish is very common.\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n=== Spice paste ===\n* 2 cloves [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]] \n* 4 [[Cookbook:Shallot|shallot]]\n* 2 cm fresh [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]] \n* 2 cm fresh [[Cookbook:Turmeric|turmeric]] \n* 50 g [[Cookbook:Chiles|fresh chile pepper]]\n* 5 [[Cookbook:Candlenut|candlenut]] \n* 5 g [[Cookbook:Tamarind|tamarind]] \n* ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 25 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]] water\n\n=== Assembly ===\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Kilogram|kg]] whole [[Cookbook:Fish|fish]] (carp or snapper)\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tomato|chopped tomato]] \n* 1 stalk [[Cookbook:Green onion|green onion]] \n* 1 stalk [[Cookbook:Lemongrass|lemongrass]] \n* 5 [[Cookbook:Bay Leaf|salam leaves]] \n* 50 g [[Cookbook:Basil|kemangi leaves]] (sweet basil; optional)\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n* 1 tsp [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Vegetable oil|salad oil]]\n* Banana leaves or [[Cookbook:Aluminium Foil|aluminum foil]] to wrap\n\n==Procedure==\n#Grind together all the ingredients for the spice paste.\n#Scale and clean the fish. Take out the intestines but not the eggs.\n#Make three diagonal slashes on each side of the fish for spice paste flavor to immerse. \n#[[Cookbook:Marinating|Marinate]] the fish with salt and tamarind for 15 minutes then wash the fish with a bowl of water to remove excess salt.\n#Add cooking oil to the spice-paste, mix. \n#Coat fish with spice paste. \n#Put kemangi leaves, salam leaves and sliced lemon grass for the flavor. \n#Wrap the fish in banana leaves or aluminum foil.\n#[[Cookbook:Steaming|Steam]] over medium heat for 30 minutes. Use pressure cooker for faster cooking time and better taste. \n#Let it cool and [[Cookbook:Grilling|grill]] the wrapped fish over charcoal fire.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using carp]]\n[[Category:Indonesian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using candlenut]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fresh ginger]]\n[[Category:Recipes using salt]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green onion]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemongrass]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Pepes Ikan (Indonesian Steamed Fish)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"4–6","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 cloves garlic","sourceText":"2 cloves garlic","amountText":"2 cloves garlic","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"4 shallot","sourceText":"4 shallot","amountText":"4 shallot","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"2 cm fresh ginger","sourceText":"2 cm fresh ginger","amountText":"2 cm fresh ginger","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"2 cm fresh turmeric","sourceText":"2 cm fresh turmeric","amountText":"2 cm fresh turmeric","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"50 g fresh chile pepper","sourceText":"50 g fresh chile pepper","amountText":"50 g fresh chile pepper","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"5 candlenut","sourceText":"5 candlenut","amountText":"5 candlenut","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"5 g tamarind","sourceText":"5 g tamarind","amountText":"5 g tamarind","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"½ tsp salt","sourceText":"½ tsp salt","amountText":"½ tsp salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"25 ml water","sourceText":"25 ml water","amountText":"25 ml water","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-10","name":"1 kg whole fish (carp or snapper)","sourceText":"1 kg whole fish (carp or snapper)","amountText":"1 kg whole fish (carp